{
  "id": "navigation/constructor_calls/04_aliases_and_deduction",
  "topic": "navigation",
  "subtopic": "constructor_calls",
  "title": "Aliases and deduction",
  "summary": "A construction through an alias or a deduced template leads to its constructor",
  "prose": "`Alias(1)` calls the constructor of the class the alias names, and `Box(2)`\nthe constructor of the specialization its arguments deduce: both lead\nthere, go-to-type-definition to the type. `Box c(3)` declares a variable\nwhose declarator is the call: `Box` names the class, and the parenthesis\nleads to the constructor.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "struct Widget {\n    Widget(int size);\n};\n\nusing Alias = Widget;\n\ntemplate <typename T>\nstruct Box {\n    Box(T value);\n};\n\nvoid build() {\n    auto a = Alias(1);\n    auto b = Box(2);\n    Box c(3);\n}\n",
